Subject: vm, api: add shared file overlays for linear memory

A linear memory is one private anonymous mapping, so no part of it can
be shared with another instance: MAP_SHARED inside a guest is a
fiction maintained by copying. Let the sys backend replace
page-aligned ranges of a WasmMmap with MAP_FIXED|MAP_SHARED file
mappings and later restore them to fresh private anonymous pages,
exposed as overlay_shared_file and restore_private_anonymous on
Memory. The caller keeps the range unaccessed while it is replaced;
the overlay otherwise behaves as ordinary memory, with the file
providing the shared identity. A grow that would have to move the
allocation fails while any overlay exists: moving would silently turn
the shared pages into private copies.

